{"id": "EUVD-2026-103024", "enisaUuid": "2bb51f89-98b7-3955-9f6d-058b730c1904", "description": "SGLang through 0.5.21 trusts caller-supplied mm_hashes values as the multimodal prefix-cache key, allowing remote attackers to poison cached KV entries across requests. Attackers can send a different image under a known or predicted hash via /generate to disclose another request's image content or corrupt victims' responses.", "datePublished": "2026-10-16T17:38:44", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T19:24:54", "baseScore": 6.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:H/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:L/VI:L/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/issues/44641", "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/v0.5.21/python/sglang/srt/managers/tokenizer_manager.py#L1183-L1215", "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/v0.5.21/python/sglang/srt/managers/io_struct.py#L205-L215", "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/pull/44653", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/sglang-through-0.5.21-kv-cache-poisoning-via-mm-hashes-in-generate"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-111392", "GHSA-fgff-m398-2gh5"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1056c1d2-00bf-300f-bf49-84a6ace968d7", "product": {"name": "sglang", "vendor": {"name": "sgl-project"}}, "product_version": "0.5.13 \u22640.5.21"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "bd016d6d-1df7-312e-b3bc-05a468e45199", "vendor": {"name": "sgl-project"}}], "isExploited": false}